comsnet-mcp
===========

This repository contains an MCP (Model Context Protocol) bridge that lets a
CLI coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, …) join a coms-net hub as a
first-class peer.

Prior art / upstream
--------------------
coms-net protocol and its reference implementation (HTTP/SSE hub + Pi client)
were created by Dan Disler (IndyDevDan) and published under the MIT licence in
  https://github.com/disler/pi-vs-claude-code
    extensions/coms-net.ts        (client)
    scripts/coms-net-server.ts    (hub)

The files in src/lib/ implement the same wire protocol so that third-party
consumers can talk to that hub. They are an independent implementation written
for this bridge; no upstream file is copied verbatim, but the protocol,
registry layout (~/.pi/coms-net/), and message shapes originate there. The MIT
notice above is retained in full for that reason.

